    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="0691" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg595"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peirce to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 249.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Hitchcock’s No. 238 of
                    January 21 in relation to a proposed exhibition of American machinery and other
                    products illustrative of the progress of industry in the United States, I have
                    the honor to inclose herewith copy and translation of the reply of the Imperial
                    Government to Mr. Hitchcock’s note on the subject, copy of <pb facs="0692"
                        n="596" xml:id="pg596"/> which was inclosed in his No. 238, and of my note
                    of this date, pointing out that the proposition was not to hold here a permanent
                    American exposition but to exhibit for a brief space of time such products as
                    would illustrate America’s industrial progress.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D.
                    Peirce.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d589-a1.xml" xpointer="d589-a1"/>
